card.statement:
Let $U$ be a Galois ring over $\Gamma,$ $\Ga$ a noetherian algebra which is a right Harish-Chandra subalgebra of $U$, $\sm\in \Specm
\Gamma,$ such that $\cM_{\sm}$ is finite, $S=S(\sm,\sm).$ If $U=U\sm$ then for every $k\geq1$ there exist $\gamma_{k}\in \Gamma\setminus \sm$, $v_{j}\in U$, $\nu_{j}\in \sm^{k}$, $j=1,\dots,N$ such that

\begin{equation}
\gamma_{k}=\sum_{j=1}^{N} v_{j}\nu_{j}
\end{equation}

and $\supp v_{j}\in S$, $j=1,\dots,n$.
